Keep one engineering ticket per established problem. Count unique report IDs,
and preserve every report's source and body.

## Current rule

[Decision 0002 and the #4471 review](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) replace
the subject-only rule in [historical decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject).

1. Use normalized subjects to find candidates.
2. Read the report and verify tenant locale, booking form and channel.
3. Merge only if the behavior and context support the same cause.
4. If the tenant is unknown or the body conflicts with the proposed cause, keep it separate for investigation.
5. Deduplicate export overlaps by report ID; do not count every JSON row as a new report.

<Callout kind="warn">
Matching subjects are not sufficient evidence. Different subjects do not rule out one cause.
When unsure, preserve the evidence and investigate before merging.
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

The explorer runs the supplied tenant/channel classifier. Its output is a candidate cohort,
not a substitute for reading the body. See the review's unresolved timing observations.

## Current product status

The [engineering update](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause#engineering-update) reports
#4471 closed: parser fixed; booking-v3 hint not planned because that form was retired.
The explorer represents the historical export, including retired booking-v3 paths.
Check the current tenant form before applying that historical classification to new reports.
